From 3955f61af4b8f9ab66142d336c7a0184500c3b6b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dimas2211 <rodrigodimas2211@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 13:48:50 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(gym): complete trainer attendance workflow, session
 activities and notes

GYM-4A/4B. Trainer operations on top of the existing booking engine, with
no schema changes or migrations:

- "Mi agenda" in /dashboard/classes, resolved with the LIVE role and the
  active Trainer linked to the user (today/upcoming/past, gym-local date).
- Trainer attendance through GymBookingService.recordAttendance on the
  TRAINER channel; the engine now also requires the assigned Trainer to
  be active (trainerOwnsSession), checked under the session lock.
- GymBookingService.updateTrainingNotes: private notes (R36) on an
  existing attendance without faking a check-in; shares the attendance
  lock protocol (lockAttendanceTarget). Events carry no note text.
- Session (ScheduledClassActivity) and individual (ClassAttendanceActivity)
  activities: FOR SHARE locks in the global order, natural-key
  idempotency, activity_name snapshot, add-only.
- getScheduledClassById selects attendance explicitly (no training_notes).

canManageClass, requireMembershipManager and role capabilities are
unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
